  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nThe upper shortwave will be slow to move out of the region and will \nallow rain showers to persist through much of Friday as well, though \nlighter amounts and rainfall rates are expected by this point. Upper \nflow will become more southwesterly by the weekend as upper ridging \nbuilds slightly. Another upper disturbance looks possible early next \nweek. An upper low will move into the coast of southern California \nby late Sunday and will phase with an upper trough moving over the \nPacific Northwest. While some rainfall does look possible with this \nnext system, there is still a potential for dry-slotting. A cold \nfront looks to follow behind this system as it moves past the FA by \nlate next week.",
